  "notes": "V9: mobile data. Every download goes through one cache shared by the server and every zet command: a copy young enough is used, ZET is asked 'has it changed?' (304, no body), gzip. The live feed every 20 s only while a page is on screen; 5 min by day and 15 at night with none. The 13 MB timetable is checked once a day by a HEAD and downloaded only when ZET changes it; zet update no longer forces it. News feeds the same way. zet data and the Data card in Settings show today's use. V8: zet alone is the server.",
